      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.2 Adverbs"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.6.2 Top"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>far up; also loudly</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 313 occurrences, first GEN.1.20; Childs 2000, p. 53: cóó-cóó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="còòlan_172">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>còòlan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="lan"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="còòlan_172_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>mensonge(s)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>lies, falsehood</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5 Communication"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3 Behavior"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 108 occurrences, first GEN.42.12; Childs 2000, p. 53: còòláŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cowvo_173">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cowvo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="cowvo_173_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>rat palmiste</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>ground squirrel</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>a large rat; opossum (Liberian English)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 137: Tyowvo; Childs 2000, p. 54: còúwó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Dans la Bible, cowvo est un homonyme sans rapport (1SA.8.12, EXO.20.25).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cua_174">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cua</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>cuaa</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>cuanin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="cua_174_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>prendre ; (cua haki) commettre (un péché)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>take; (cua haki) commit (a sin)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.4.3 Get"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.4 Handle something"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>take; also carry, lift; take in marriage</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1496 occurrences, first GEN.2.15; Childs 2000, p. 60: cùàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cua mamaa_175">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cua mamaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="cua mamaa_175_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>petit-fils, petite-fille</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>grandchild</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.1.9 Kinship"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 134: Tyua mamaa; Childs 2000, p. 60: cùàà-màmàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Sens confirmé par Childs (cùàà-màmàá). Dans la Bible, mamaa désigne l'aïeul (Gn 28,13) et cuavaa-imamaa « les descendants ». Mots attestés séparément dans la Bible, mais pas cette expression.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cuaa_176">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cuaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>cuavaa</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>cuawva</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="cuaa_176_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>enfant ; la femme (dont on parle) ; (pl.) enfants, descendants</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>child; the woman (in question); (pl.) children, descendants</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.1.9 Kinship"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.6.5 Male, female"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>girl, daughter, young woman, woman</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 270 occurrences, first GEN.3.13; Childs 2000, p. 60: cùàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Au singulier, la Bible emploie cuaa surtout pour « la femme » dont il est question (Gn 3,13 ; 1 S 1,26 ; 2 R 8,6) ; le pluriel cuavaa / cuawva signifie « enfants, descendants ». À vérifier auprès de locuteurs.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cuaa_177">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cuaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>cua</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>cue</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>cuanin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>cuenin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="cuaa_177_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>prendre</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>take</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.4 Handle something"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.4.3 Get"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>take, carry or lift</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 115: Tyuaa; Childs 2000, p. 60: cùàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>cua est très courant (GEN 2,15) ; cue, cuenin : radical négatif. La forme longue cuaa de la Bible a surtout d'autres sens (« femme », GEN 3,13).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cuaambɔyɛi_178">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cuaambɔyɛi</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="cuaambɔyɛi_178_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>jeunesse</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>youth</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.6.4 Stage of life"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 13 occurrences, first GEN.46.34</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cuaambɔɔ_179">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cuaambɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>cuaambɔa</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>cuaambɔ</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="cuaambɔɔ_179_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>jeune fille, fille ; jeune (personne) ; jeune (garçon ou fille), jeune fille</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>girl, young woman; young person</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.6.4 Stage of life"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>girl</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 56 occurrences, first GEN.16.5; Keita 1979, p. 148: Tyuaamböö; Childs 2000, p. 61: cùààmbɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita : « l'enfant » ; dans la Bible, surtout « jeune fille » (Rébecca, Gn 24,18), opposé à kaasonɔɔ « adulte ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cuei_180">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cuei</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>cueon</text></form></field>
    <sense id="cuei_180_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>hache</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>axe</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.7.1 Cutting tool"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 17 occurrences, first DEU.19.5; Keita 1979, p. 160: Tyuei; Childs 2000, p. 61: cùèí</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cuello_181">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cuello</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>cuel</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="cuello_181_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>prendre pour quelqu'un</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>take for someone</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.4.3 Get"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 2 occurrences, first 1SA.14.6; Keita 1979, p. 114: Tyuello</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Bénéfactif de cuaa (radical cue) : cuel lanɔɔ « prendre une femme pour » (GEN 24,4).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cuinndo_182">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cuinndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>cuinnda</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>cuin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>cuinaa</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="cuinndo_182_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>chèvre</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>goat</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.3.1 Domesticated animal"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 8 occurrences, first GEN.21.14; Keita 1979, p. 137: Tyuinndo; Childs 2000, p. 63: cùìŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>La Bible a aussi le pluriel cuinaa.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
